    "message": "fix(routing): make model refs readable on the routing cards\n\nThe routing cards clipped the thing they exist to show. Measured on a 1500px\nwindow, four cards fitted the row at 365px each, which left 169px for the\nmodel ref and truncated 16 of 18 of them mid-name -- `nous_portal/meit`,\n`chatgpt_oauth/gp`. The reorder arrows shipped in 5.37.0 made it slightly\nworse, because the primary field now carries a button cluster too.\n\nTwo changes, in the order they matter:\n\n1. Fewer, wider cards. `.route-grid` asks for 460px rather than 360px, so\n   three rails fit that window instead of four and each card gets 491px.\n\n2. The chrome around the text is trimmed to what it needs. The three row\n   buttons drop 30px -> 26px wide (height untouched, so the target stays\n   30px tall), the marker column 26px -> 24px, row gaps 6px -> 4px, the\n   card's side padding 20px -> 14px, and the combobox chevron's reserved\n   gutter 44px -> 28px with the field's own inset 14px -> 10px.\n\nResult at the same window: 337px of field, 0 of 18 refs clipped, including\n`nvidia_nim/nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b` which is the longest a default\ninstall can produce.\n\nThe button rules had to be written against the `.route-rail`-scoped\noverrides, not the generic `.model-chain-*` ones. The generic rules are\nshadowed on this page, so editing them changes nothing here -- a first pass\ndid exactly that and measured as a no-op.\n\nAlso: every model field now carries a `title` equal to its value, so a ref\nlonger than the field is recoverable by hovering rather than only by clicking\nin and scrolling. That is what covers a user whose provider names run longer\nthan mine, instead of tuning the pixel budget to my own longest model name.\nReorders assign `.value` directly, which fires no event, so they now dispatch\n`change` -- otherwise the title (and the dirty state) would go stale after a\nswap.\n\nVerification\n------------\nMeasured in a real browser (Chrome DevTools) against a real server at the\nreported 1506px grid width, on a config seeded to match the report:\n\n    before   4 cols   365px card   169px field   16/18 clipped (worst 179px short)\n    A only   3 cols   491px card   295px field    3/18 clipped\n    final    3 cols   491px card   337px field    0/18 clipped\n\nRail alignment re-checked inside one card after resizing the marker column:\nmarker, all three row numbers and the add \"+\" share a centre at 27px.\nTooltips present on 18/18 fields.\n\nThe 5.37.0 reorder harness re-run against this build: 29/29 passing. It first\nreported 6 failures against the seeded server -- that was the harness assuming\nan empty config, not a regression; re-run against an empty home it is green.\n\nLocal CI: ruff format --check, ruff check, ty clean; pytest 4795 passed with\nthe documented 6 test_install_ps1_* baseline failures.\n\nNot done\n--------\nNo new guard test. The existing class guard already fails if these rules are\nlost in a merge, and a test asserting specific pixel values would encode my\nwindow rather than any invariant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Y6SPhyApg7trDx44SJqNti",
